  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The default settings of the VRC Spatial Audio Source component are not great.\nWith the default Near of 0, a dramatic amount of falloff occurs just in the range between two players in close proximity. New creators are often confused as to why their audio sources are so quiet.\nThe default Far of 40 is an incredibly large distance, representing the width of the entire map in many cases.\nDefaults of something like 5 Near and 10 or 15 Far would ensure that audio sources are at a good volume for nearby players but drop off over a much more reasonable distance.",
